        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0853d1481c4149f695a579114df4f4d5",
      "statement": "resolve() returns the constructed spec instances in the requested names order, and the requested list must be rank-symmetric: every DDP rank has to request the identical list because torchrun and Lightning hand every rank the same CLI arguments, so an asymmetric list is a never-observed manual-scripting failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L73-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4b2443053e896efe4a367a1e257a081625d88a47057e11c5419312bacb7dd091:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_61e2e5ea518944a3ad912f98494c1ca2",
      "statement": "validate_monitor runs after resolve/build and before the trainer is built: it is a no-op when no checkpoint spec is present or the monitor_metric is None, and otherwise the monitor must appear in the union of every spec's logged_metrics, the module's logged_metrics, and every extra callback's logged_metrics, raising ValueError with the available set when nobody logs it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/registry.py#L114-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af95f5276d1be7a22b7e75a5b7011bdbe4161b0dcf37dda3ba850149d5855b7e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_60a4371a00c245029b7dad1627836615",
      "statement": "TrainingSpine.run is the single caller of the registry and merges in this order: default names (or the callback_names_override that replaces them) → forbidden_callbacks force-removal after the merge → forbidden_monitors rejection of a forbidden checkpoint monitor before resolution → resolve → build → extra callbacks appended → validate_monitor → ModelCheckpoint presence check → build_trainer → trainer.fit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/core.py#L42-L162",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1dd42fd3ea9705af9c779b202fadfc2e98f98f7fb61f231634d6540dc59a9535:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a36a1647693841e7b909cda3aa74e35d",
      "statement": "Each training shell derives its own default callback-name list: JiT ['train_loss', 'fid', 'checkpoint'] (fid only when FID is attached), reward ['checkpoint'], GRPO ['checkpoint'] plus 'fid' when the FID triple is active, and the supervised ControlNet shell ['train_loss', 'checkpoint', 'paired_fidelity'].",
      "evidence": [
